  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1043 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nA weak ridge will bring benign conditions and continued cooler \ntemperatures as 500 mb heights remain relatively low. A quasi-split \nupper flow will develop over the Desert Southwest early Saturday. \nLeading shortwaves out ahead of it will propagate over southern \nportions of our area and bring precipitation chances in the mainly \nmorning as well with increased mid-level Pacific moisture advection \ngiven the overall upper trough orientation. It remains somewhat \nuncertain how far north this will reach, however even if the \nsomewhat later ECMWF verifies, it would be more rain than thunder \nand move out relatively quickly. Another disturbance may track to \nthe east on Sunday, but conditions look to remain dry. Temperatures \nwill slowly increase next week as a ridge builds in from the west.",
